# .trivyignore — documented, justified exceptions for the image CVE scan (v9.138).
# Each entry MUST carry a justification and a re-evaluation trigger. The Trivy CI
# job gates on FIXABLE CRITICAL after applying this file; an undocumented add here
# is a review smell. HIGH findings are reported informationally, not gated.
# Each exception is also declared, with the same reason, in vex.openvex.json (OpenVEX).

# CVE-2025-68121 — Go crypto/tls: incorrect certificate validation during TLS
# session resumption. Present in /usr/local/bin/gosu (the Go stdlib it was
# compiled with) inside the postgres:16-alpine base image. gosu is the postgres
# entrypoint's privilege-drop helper; it opens NO TLS connection, so the
# vulnerable session-resumption path is unreachable. The CVE rides in across
# postgres:16-alpine and postgres:17-alpine (same gosu binary) and is not
# addressable by apk upgrade (gosu is not an apk package) or a base bump.
# Re-evaluate when the postgres base ships a gosu rebuilt with Go >= 1.24.13.
CVE-2025-68121

# CVE-2026-56857 (GO-2026-6604): Go os, Root.Mkdir and Root.MkdirAll can follow
# junctions out of the root on Windows. Present in /usr/local/bin/gosu (the Go 1.24.6
# stdlib it was compiled with) inside the postgres:16-alpine base image. The Go
# vulnerability database limits every vulnerable symbol (in os and
# internal/syscall/windows) to GOOS windows, and this gosu is built for linux and links
# no os.Root symbol (go tool nm), so the vulnerable code is not in it. gosu is not an
# apk package, so apk upgrade cannot
# replace it. The Caddy edge, which this repository compiles, is built with Go
# 1.26.10 instead (polaris_web/Dockerfile.caddy).
# An ID here is global: it also covers this CVE in every other image the gate scans,
# and the Windows-only limit holds for each of them, since every image we scan is linux.
# Re-evaluate when the postgres base ships a gosu rebuilt with Go >= 1.26.9.
CVE-2026-56857
